  "question": {
    "text": "A diatomic gas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> does <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> of work when it is expanded isobarically. The heat given to the gas in the process is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1400",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For&nbsp;isobaric process:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>T</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>400</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>T</mi></math></p><p>Also:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>T</mi></math>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>T</mi></math>&nbsp; (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, for diatomic gas)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>400</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p>"
  }
